<title>USA: Oglethorpe County, Ga., plans June tax referendum.</title>
<headline>Oglethorpe County, Ga., plans June tax referendum.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Ga 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia's Oglethorpe County has scheduled a June 17 referendum on a proposal to extend its local-option sales tax for five years, the Athens Banner Herald said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The one-cent sales tax raised $468,000 last year and is scheduled to expire on Sept. 30. County officials said if the extension is rejected, property taxes would hav eto be raised by 3 mills to offset the revenue loss.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
